# ArchiveXL manifest for JackieLives (v1.71) — the ONLY thing this archive does is make a female V,
# and a Jackie talking TO a female V, sound right.
#
# WHY AN ARCHIVE AT ALL, IN A MOD THAT HAS NEVER SHIPPED ONE
# A line's male and female takes share ONE String ID. `locVoiceoverMap` holds a PAIR of paths and the
# ENGINE picks the column, natively — `audioDialogLineEventData` has no gender field, `AudioSystem`
# has no gender argument, and there is exactly one `v` voice tag. So no amount of Lua or redscript can
# ask for a take. The only lever is to put the recording we want behind a String ID of our OWN.
# Full investigation: ../NCLives/docs/research/vo_gender.md.
#
# `vomaps:` is undocumented — ArchiveXL's wiki lists only `onscreens` — but its source defines four
# keys (onscreens, subtitles, lipmaps, vomaps) in src/App/Extensions/Localization/Config.cpp:6-10, and
# OnLoadVoiceOvers (Extension.cpp:327) MERGES what we name here into the game's voiceover index:
#
#     entry.voMapChunks.PushBack(ref);
#
# Merged, not replaced. Our map holds 47 rows of our own synthetic ids — 41 of V's lines and 6 of
# Jackie's "chica"/"mano" pairs — each pointing both columns at the vanilla FEMALE .wem. It contains
# only String IDs and depot paths: no audio, no CDPR text, nothing of theirs redistributed. Patching
# their map instead would have meant shipping 30,184 of their entries (4.19 MB) to change 47.
#
# `onscreens:` is ONE string, and it is not player-facing. It is a BEACON: JackieLives has no journal
# to look for, so `jlArchiveLoaded()` asks the game for this key. Without a detector we could not tell
# "archive missing" from "wrong gender", and speaking a synthetic id with no archive is SILENCE —
# strictly worse than the male take. Do not delete it thinking it is dead content.
#
# ⚠️ en-us ONLY. The .wem paths under en-us\vo\ are the English recordings. A player on another
# language keeps the male takes, which is exactly what they have today — vo.lua falls back whenever an
# id isn't mapped, so this can never mute a line.
#
# ⚠️ Build with `python tools\build_archive.py` on WINDOWS (WolvenKit CLI). The generated sources come
# from `python3 tools/gen_vomap.py` on the MAC, which reads the installed game.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# v1.92 — HE TEXTS YOU. `journal:` MERGES our conversation into the game's own journal tree rather
# than replacing it, by id chain: existing containers are descended into and unknown children are
# appended. That is the only reason a modded thread can hang under a CDPR contact at all, and why
# this cannot conflict with the Panam Romance Messages mod, the Rita addon, or NCLives.
#
# Jackie is ALREADY a vanilla contact (`contacts/jackie`, five prologue conversations). We add ONE
# new conversation under him, `jackielives`, so the thread wears his real face and his real name.
# Verified against PRME, which does exactly this to vanilla panam/mitch/saul and leaves their
# vanilla threads working.
#
# ⚠️ Journal entries carry only LocKeys. Without the onscreens file below the phone renders raw
# `LocKey#<id>` strings — that is the ONLY symptom of a wrong hash, so there is nothing else to look
# for. See tools/gen_messages.py's fnv1a64().
#
# v2.0 — THE QUESTLINE. The second journal carries the tracked quests, their phases and objectives
# ("Ghost in the Machine" plus the Heywood side jobs) and the readable shards. Same merge-by-id-chain
# rule as above, so it appends into `quests/` and `onscreens/` rather than replacing either.
# Generated by tools/gen_journal_quests.py from storyboard.lua + sidequests.lua.
journal:
  - mod\jackielives\journal\jackielives_messages.journal
  - mod\jackielives\journal\jackielives_quests.journal

localization:
  vomaps:
    en-us: mod\jackielives\vomaps\en-us\jackielives_vomap.json
  onscreens:
    # ⚠️ A LIST PER LOCALE, AND THE TWO FILES ARE NOT INTERCHANGEABLE. ArchiveXL accepts either a
    # single resource path or a list (src/App/Extensions/Localization/Config.cpp, "resource path or
    # list of paths"); NCLives has relied on the list form since v1.45.
    #
    # ⚠️⚠️ jackielives_onscreens.json IS NOT PLAYER-FACING TEXT AND MUST NOT BE REMOVED OR REUSED.
    # It carries exactly one string, `jl_vomap_token` — the archive-presence beacon that
    # jlArchiveLoaded() reads, and whose value is the voice map's version fingerprint. It is written
    # by tools/gen_vomap.py. If the message text were ever generated into THAT filename instead of
    # its own, the beacon would be silently overwritten, jlArchiveLoaded() would return false
    # forever, and VO.femaleTakeId would refuse to substitute all 47 female-take ids — which reads
    # in game as a voice bug, not as a messages bug. That is why the SMS text lives in
    # jackielives_msgs.json, a separate stem, generated by a separate tool.
    en-us:
      - mod\jackielives\onscreens\en-us\jackielives_onscreens.json   # the vomap beacon — DO NOT REMOVE
      - mod\jackielives\onscreens\en-us\jackielives_msgs.json        # the SMS text
      - mod\jackielives\questtext\en-us\jackielives_questtext.json   # quest + objective + shard text
    # One line per additional locale, msgs only: the beacon is en-us and language-independent.
    ja-jp:
      - mod\jackielives\onscreens\ja-jp\jackielives_msgs.json
      - mod\jackielives\questtext\ja-jp\jackielives_questtext.json
